<!--BlockML Core — root Block type

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.core.Block-->
<core:Block xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:bml="org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition">

  <is>
    A semantic building block
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Root semantic unit of BlockML — the sole inheritance root for all Block definitions.
    Every concept in the grammar is a Block: composable domain types, ValueTypes, Languages,
    Status values, Constraints, Capabilities, Exceptions, Services, Libraries, and Definition meta-model
    types. Unqualified name Block resolves to this type.
    
    Role and constraints:
    • Sole inheritance root — omits &lt;baseType>; all other definitions must declare a non-empty parent FQN
    • Package org.blockml.bml.core — every root Block in this package must inherit directly from
      this type. Nested Sub-Blocks in core are exempt (doc:ModelingGuidelines)
    • Abstract — not used directly as a composition instance type
    • Further members defined by sub-types — Properties, Aggregations,
      Associations, and Capabilities via the baseType chain
    • Composition instance identity uses bml:id and bml:version (not member attributes)
    • Documentation prose language is Definition meta (def:BlockDefinition.language), not a
      member of this type — this document authors &lt;language>&lt;English/>&lt;/language> as the
      framework default for inheritance
    
    Type reference rules:
    • Aggregation member types may be any Block FQN
    • Association member types must be InstanceReference(T) or InstanceReference(T)[]
    • Property and Capability payload types must resolve to a ValueType
    • Capability throws lists Exception types via TypeReferenceEntity — not ValueType payloads
    • Capability implementation language attributes reference org.blockml.bml.language.* — unqualified names permitted
    
    Documentation model (on every root block definition — see def:BlockDefinition /
    doc:DocumentationModel):
    • Definition identity first — element type/name tag (preferred) or &lt;name> / &lt;type> /
      &lt;baseType> (baseType omitted only here; dual format: doc:DocumentFormat)
    • &lt;is> — always required after identity; clear Urbild designation (what the Block semantically represents)
    • &lt;summary> — required when documentation is too long for a quick scan
    • &lt;language> — optional Definition meta; natural language for documentation prose
      (inherits from enclosing Library document, then this Block document's English default)
    • &lt;documentation> — always required; technical description; optional language
      attribute when prose deviates from effective block language
    • &lt;isNot> — required when confusion risk exists
    • Optional extensions: &lt;since>, &lt;changelog>, &lt;examples>, &lt;references>
    Omitted is or documentation → BML_MISSING_IS / BML_MISSING_DOCUMENTATION; missing isNot or
    summary when required → BML_MISSING_IS_NOT / BML_MISSING_SUMMARY (warning V1).
    
    Serialization:
    • bml:xml ${ bml:Self } — composable instances render under their declared type tag
      (for example &lt;core:Block>, &lt;myns:Wall>)
    • Definition branch types describe block structure and carry their own bml:xml rules
  </documentation>
  <abstract>
    true
  </abstract>
  <references>
    <see type="core:ValueType" relation="Extends">
      Property and capability payload types.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Language" relation="Extends">
      Implementation language bindings and NaturalLanguage branch.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Status" relation="Extends">
      Lifecycle status references.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Relation" relation="Extends">
      Cross-reference relationship categories on see entries.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Constraint" relation="Extends">
      Property validation constraints.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Capability" relation="Extends">
      Capability implementation contracts.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Exception" relation="Extends">
      Capability-thrown exception types listed on throws.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Definition" relation="Extends">
      Meta-model for block structure (WIP).
    </see>
    <see type="def:BlockDefinition" aggregation="language" relation="Defines">
      Definition meta — documentation prose language on every Block document.
    </see>
    <see type="def:StructuralDefinition" relation="Defines">
      Shared documentation model for structural definition elements.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:DocumentFormat" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Type/name as element tag on root, Sub-Blocks, and embeds.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:DocumentationModel" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Block documentation model — is, documentation, extensions.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:DefinitionModel" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Root type exception and Definition branch.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:ModelingGuidelines" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Core package: root Blocks must be direct children of Block; Sub-Blocks exempt.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:EverythingIsABlock" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Everything is a Block — type system overview.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:BmlDirectives" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Definition branch bml:xml serialization rules.
    </see>
  </references>
  <language>
    <org.blockml.bml.language.English />
  </language>
  <bml:xml>${ bml:Self }</bml:xml>
</core:Block>
